 "insight": [
  "The non-EU partners that changed their import ranking positions the most between 2005 and 2025 are Viet Nam, Japan, and Türkiye.",
  "Viet Nam's imports increased from 164 thousand euros in 2005 to 17.5 million euros in 2025, a rise of 10,579.7%.",
  "Japan's imports grew from 127.5 million euros to 1.13 billion euros, increasing by 783.9%.",
  "In contrast, imports from China decreased significantly from 2.25 billion euros in 2005 to 761.3 million euros in 2025, a drop of 66.1%.",
  "These values are nominal and not adjusted for price changes, and the United Kingdom is counted as extra-EU throughout the period."
 ],
